WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.510 --> 00:00:08.149
Shops in the Venezuelan capital smashed up
and picked clean of their contents...

00:00:08.149 --> 00:00:13.370
At this supermarket in southeastern Caracas,
people accused of taking food including pasta,

00:00:13.370 --> 00:00:21.240
rice and tomato sauce were among those later
arrested by security forces for looting.

00:00:21.240 --> 00:00:27.050
Scenes of desperation like this are becoming
more commonplace in the crisis-hit South American

00:00:27.050 --> 00:00:38.989
nation... compounded by a days-long power
outage.

00:00:38.989 --> 00:00:41.769
Medicines were already in short supply.

00:00:41.769 --> 00:00:47.399
Now reports that the blackout has led to patients
dying in hospitals are also fuelling rising

00:00:47.399 --> 00:00:49.719
anger at the government's inaction.

00:00:49.719 --> 00:00:56.709
The crisis in Venezuela has a first and last
name and it is Nicolas Maduro ((... )) It's

00:00:56.709 --> 00:01:02.251
time to understand that the humanitarian crisis
is not a political crisis, it is a social

00:01:02.251 --> 00:01:03.251
crisis.

00:01:03.251 --> 00:01:06.620
Venezuelans are dying because there are no
solutions."

00:01:06.620 --> 00:01:11.720
Meanwhile those fortunate enough to get power
from a generator are finding new uses for

00:01:11.720 --> 00:01:14.390
their refrigerators.

00:01:14.390 --> 00:01:18.940
We have a refrigerator where we're storing
food, but it can also fit some medicines.

00:01:18.940 --> 00:01:22.560
There are a lot of people that need to store
them in refrigeration, at least as far as

00:01:22.560 --> 00:01:27.730
insulin is concerned.

00:01:27.730 --> 00:01:31.240
But many businesses have been without power
for days.

00:01:31.240 --> 00:01:35.750
With their fridges off - food is rotting on
the shelves, forcing many shop-owners to cut

00:01:35.750 --> 00:01:39.820
their losses.

00:01:39.820 --> 00:01:43.740
I'm giving this all away . Yesterday I gave
away pizza.

00:01:43.740 --> 00:01:49.820
Today I'll give all this to the kids on the
street.

00:01:49.820 --> 00:01:54.350
As the crippling blackout drags on, so does
the blame game between the opposition and

00:01:54.350 --> 00:01:55.810
the president.

00:01:55.810 --> 00:01:59.560
All Venezuelans can do for now is wait for
good news.

